  "query_preview": "..Dry and stable conditions remain across the region\nwith temperatures running 5-7 degrees cooler than normal across\nnorthern Utah and near normal across southern Utah. Moisture\nstarts to advect back into Utah and SW Wyoming tomorrow as an\nupper-level low swings into the Great Basin. This low will\ninitiate convection across southern Utah late Monday with moisture\nspreading north and into northern Utah by Tuesday. PWATs approach\nthe 90th percentile for this time of year, but storm motion will\nbe fast enough to limit flooding impacts except for areas that\nexperience any training storms. Steep lapse rates and 30-50 kts \nof shear will help storms mature and stay mature. Some isolated\nstrong thunderstorms will be possible.\n\nAs the low tracks to the east conditions will become quieter\nacross most of Utah, but moisture will remain elevated across\nsoutheastern Utah through much of the week. This late monsoon\nmoisture tap will keep diurnal storm chances each day across areas\nof southeastern Utah.",
